WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.242
GROUP BY defines the grain of a summary result With
no GROUP

00:00:05.255 --> 00:00:09.823
BY an aggregate can summarize the whole table into
one row If

00:00:09.850 --> 00:00:15.100
we group by diagnosis the output becomes one row per
diagnosis If

00:00:15.126 --> 00:00:19.310
we group by patient and diagnosis the result becomes
more detailed one

00:00:19.336 --> 00:00:25.119
row per patient-and-diagnosis combination This is
why adding grouping columns

00:00:25.145 --> 00:00:30.708
usually increases the number of output rows A
beginner-friendly rule

00:00:30.721 --> 00:00:34.590
is that selected columns that are not inside
aggregate functions generally need

00:00:34.603 --> 00:00:39.521
to appear in GROUP BY But the deeper rule is about
meaning

00:00:40.458 --> 00:00:44.814
Every selected non-aggregate value should be
well-defined for the group represented by

00:00:44.827 --> 00:00:50.541
that output row Before writing GROUP BY finish the
sentence one

00:00:50.567 --> 00:00:52.409
row in my result represents one
